      "problem": "Consider the function $F(x)=|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|$ defined on $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ The Fourier series of the $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{2}{\\pi }-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{\\pi (4{n}^{2}-1)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2nx).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.At $x=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2n\\cdot 0)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is \n{{field-2}}\nat $x=0,$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(0)={{field-3}}.\n$$",
